    "articles": [
      {
        "no": 1,
        "text": {
          "en": "The Supreme People's Court\nReply on the Question of How Parties Should Be Listed in a Civil Order\nof Remand for Retrial Made by a Second-Instance People's Court on the\nGround of the Addition or Replacement of Parties\n14 April 1990      Fa Min No. 8 [1990]\nTo the Higher People's Court of Shandong Province:\nThe request for instructions and report of your court, Lu Fa (Jing) Han No. 19 [1990], on the question whether a party added in second instance should be listed in a civil ruling of remand for retrial made after mediation fails following the addition of that party, has been received. After study, we are of the opinion that:\nWhere a second-instance people's court tries a case in which parties need to be added or replaced and mediation fails, the case shall be remanded for retrial. The parties added or replaced shall not be listed in the civil ruling of remand for retrial."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 1."
        }
      }
    ]
