    "articles": [
      {
        "no": 1,
        "text": {
          "en": "Supreme People's Court\nReply on Whether a People's Court Should Accept an Administrative\nAction Brought by a Party on the Ground that the Health Administrative\nDepartment Has Failed to Perform Its Statutory Duties\n14 June 1995      Xing Ta Zi No. 6 [1995]\nTo the Higher People's Court of Anhui Province:\nThe request for instructions of your court, Wan Xing Jian Zi No. 06 [1994], has been received. After study, the reply is as follows: where the committee for the appraisal of medical accidents has made a final appraisal that the case does not constitute a medical accident and the health administrative department refuses to make a decision on handling the medical dispute, and the party concerned, on the ground of failure to perform statutory duties, brings an administrative action before a people's court in accordance with law, the people's court shall accept the case.\nThis is our reply."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 1."
        }
      }
    ]
