        "no": 1,
        "text": {
          "en": "Supreme People's Court\nReply on the Question of Applying to a People's Court for Compulsory Enforcement\nof a Specific Administrative Act Lawfully Made by a Forestry Administrative Organ\n(24 December 1993, as amended in accordance with the Decision of the Supreme People's Court on Amending Eighteen Judicial Interpretations on Enforcement Including the Provisions of the Supreme People's Court on Several Issues concerning the Seizure of Goods in Railway Transport by People's Courts, adopted at the 1,823rd meeting of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on 23 December 2020)\nTo the Ministry of Forestry:\nThe letter of your ministry, Lin Han Ce Zi No. 308 [1993], has been received. After study, this Court agrees with the opinions put forward by your ministry, namely: where, in respect of a specific administrative act lawfully made by a competent forestry department, a natural person, a legal person or an unincorporated organisation neither files a lawsuit nor performs the act within the statutory time limit, the competent forestry department may, in accordance with the provisions of Article 97 of the Administrative Litigation Law, apply to a people's court for compulsory enforcement, and the people's court shall accept the application."
        },
        "noLabel": {
          "en": "Article 1."
        }
